220-L222","doc":"The word of a normal form: its blocks, in order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.descRun","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.descRun","kind":"def","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L214-L218","doc":"`descRun i j = [i, i-1, …, j]` — the descending run one block contributes.\nEvery intermediate value is a valid `Fin m` because `i` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.elems","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.elems","kind":"def","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L208-L212","doc":"The elements of `s` in increasing order. `List.finRange` is already sorted,\nso no sorting algorithm is needed — and unlike `Finset.sort` this **reduces in\nthe kernel**, which is what makes every `decide` in this file possible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_six","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L201-L204","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_five","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L195-L198","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_four","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L189-L192","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_three","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L183-L186","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_two","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L178-L181","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_one","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L173-L176","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.card_zero","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L168-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.instFintypeNormalIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.instFintypeNormalIdx","kind":"instance","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L161-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.instDecidableEqNormalIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.instDecidableEqNormalIdx","kind":"instance","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L160-L160","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.NormalIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebNormalForm.NormalIdx","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/TemperleyLiebNormalForm.lean#L150-L158","doc":"A Jones normal form for `TL_{m+1}(δ)`, as a pair of equal-size subsets of\nthe `m` generators with `J` dominating `I`.\n\nThe domination is stated as a threshold count rather than pointwise on sorted\nlists, which is what keeps the whole type decidable. ","signatureChunk":0}]}